Blackdrift: set the Compose palette's pink and violet accents to Clean Slate.

Why: Focus's Compose screens (About, radio-button lists, dialogs, onboarding)
take colours from FocusColors in ui/theme/FocusTheme.kt, which hard-codes
Photon values, so patch 0208's XML colour mapping cannot reach them. The About
"Learn more" link, selected radio buttons and dialog controls (Photon Pink)
become Drift blue (#2F6FD6 light, #7AA8F5 dark, the same values 0208 gives
accentBright/focusContrastPink), the dark onboarding button (Violet50)
becomes dark Drift blue, and the light Material surface (Violet05 lavender)
becomes the Clean Slate surface white. This patch is hand-written: it is not
produced by branding/scripts/apply-focus-colors.mjs, so regenerating 0208
leaves it intact. It is part of the branding group (0200-0299) and
touches only FocusTheme.kt, which no other patch changes.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

